WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.940
Even strong application query design cannot protect a MongoDB deployment that is broadly exposed with weak access controls.

2
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:15.400
Use private networking, IP access controls, firewalls, security groups, or platform-equivalent network restrictions.

3
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.460
Enable access control and role-based access control with least privilege.

4
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:29.760
Separate application users, administrator users, migration users, reporting users, human users, and emergency access paths where appropriate.

5
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:34.740
Administrative access should require strong authentication and periodic review.

6
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:41.420
Keep server versions, drivers, dependencies, base images, and deployment configuration current.

7
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:48.240
Review configuration drift, emergency changes, manual console edits, and one-off operational fixes.

8
00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:53.380
They should leave evidence and be reconciled back into normal infrastructure management.

9
00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.720
Hardening is not a one-time checklist.

10
00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:06.060
It is the ongoing process of keeping the deployed database, the Node.js runtime, supporting images, and operational procedures aligned with the security model the team expects.

11
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.780
Backups deserve the same protection as production data.

12
00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:17.480
They should be encrypted where appropriate, access-controlled, covered by retention policy, tested for restore, and monitored for failure.

13
00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:25.340
Audit logs and operational logs should capture security-relevant events without exposing sensitive data unnecessarily.

14
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:35.840
Track administrative actions, privilege changes, unusual connection patterns, backup failures, restore activity, configuration changes, and suspicious access behavior.

15
00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.820
A recoverable and observable database is much easier to defend during an incident.
